          "html": "<p>B and C only </p>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p>Opposite faces </p><p>Solid black face ↔ small black square face. </p><p>Star face ↔ (inline) blank face. </p><p>Circled plus ( ⊕ ) face ↔ (side) blank face. </p><p>Rule: Opposite faces can’t touch (can’t be seen adjacent on the same cube). </p><p>Elimination </p><p>B: shows the solid black face adjacent to the small black square → opposites adjacent ⇒ impossible . </p><p>D: again places solid black next to the small black square → opposites adjacent ⇒ impossible . </p>",
